5. An ant takes one more fry, leaving five behind.
- (1/3)Z - 1 = 5.
Now, we can start solving the equation from the bottom up.
Before the pigeons ate, there were 18 + 9 = 27 fries.
The seagull ate 7 fries, so before the seagull ate, there were 27 + 7 = 34 fries.
Dave bought a pack and ate 14 fries, leaving 34, so the initial number of fries when Dave bought it was 34 + 14.
